<h2 class="doc-h2">Action</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Keep it to an undo or a link. A toast disappears, so anything that <i>has</i> to be done
    cannot live only in one.
</p>
<Example Source="ToastAction.razor"><ToastAction /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Promise</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Sonner's <code>toast.promise</code> follows a pending fetch. There is no fetch to follow here:
    a form posts and the server answers, and the honest equivalent is for the handler that did the
    work to raise the toast — one header, no client state, and no way for the two to disagree
    about whether it succeeded.
</p>
